WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.833
This is the PyCUBRID team demo.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:04.943
First, pycubrid.

00:00:04.943 --> 00:00:09.873
In a fresh virtual environment, one
pip install line is all it takes.

00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:15.106
A first query.

00:00:15.106 --> 00:00:20.063
Open a connection, create a
cursor and run SELECT 1 + 1.

00:00:20.063 --> 00:00:22.985
Run the file and the result is 2.

00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:32.571
The same code works asynchronously.

00:00:32.571 --> 00:00:34.051
Import pycubrid.

00:00:34.051 --> 00:00:38.306
aio and run it with await
for the same result.

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:41.215
Next, sqlalchemy-cubrid.

00:00:41.215 --> 00:00:47.031
Install it with pip and write the
engine URL as cubrid+pycubrid.

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:58.954
Declare the model the way
you always do with the ORM.

00:00:58.954 --> 00:01:03.928
Create the table, insert two rows
and query them: keyboard and mouse.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.381
Migrations work too.

00:01:14.381 --> 00:01:21.774
Initialize Alembic, create a revision and
upgrade, and the tag table is created and

00:01:21.774 --> 00:01:22.397
listed.

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:29.557
Third, cubrid-mcp-server.

00:01:29.557 --> 00:01:36.886
Ask an AI agent which tables exist and
it calls tools to read the table list and

00:01:36.886 --> 00:01:37.802
structure.

00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:44.351
Ask for product counts per category and the
agent writes a SELECT query, runs it and

00:01:44.351 --> 00:01:46.238
sums up the result in a table.

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:51.822
Writes are blocked by default.

00:01:51.822 --> 00:01:55.280
Ask the agent to drop a
table and it declines.

00:01:56.233 --> 00:01:58.752
The server's demo script behaves the same.

00:01:58.752 --> 00:02:02.529
The write tool is not listed,
and the drop attempt is rejected.

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:07.453
Last, cubrid-cookbook-python.

00:02:07.453 --> 00:02:14.296
Starting the database and API with Docker
Compose takes about two minutes, so this

00:02:14.296 --> 00:02:16.048
part is shown at 12x.

00:02:16.048 --> 00:02:18.718
When healthy, we send a request.

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:33.403
In the Swagger UI, the POST
request also returns 200.

00:02:40.633 --> 00:02:46.447
The repository has example directories
such as agent, async worker, batch,

00:02:46.447 --> 00:02:48.646
dashboard, Django and Flask.

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:52.961
Install commands and the
repository are on screen.

00:02:52.961 --> 00:02:54.830
The voice is AI-generated.
